(* THE PROPERTY. Expected: FALSE.

   "After the content write fails, the status must never be reported as
   Submitted for grading."

   This is the whole of APP_PARTIAL_SUBMISSION. save_submission() in
   mod/assign/locallib.php has no delegated transaction around the status row
   (m_assign_submission) and the content row (m_assignsubmission_onlinetext),
   so a status committed over content that never landed is exactly the
   non-atomic write the case study is about.

   FALSE here means the specification does not permit the counter-example --
   which is what makes observing it against the real SUT a conformance FAIL
   rather than merely an unexpected value.

   The (not SAVE_SUBMISSION)* segment matters: without it the formula would
   also match a later, SUCCESSFUL save legitimately reaching SUBMITTED_FG, and
   would report TRUE for a model that is perfectly correct. It restricts the
   search to the window between this fault and any fresh attempt.

   NOTE this is a statement about the MODEL, not about Moodle. Whether Moodle
   advances the status is decided by running tc_app_partial_submission, and
   was measured separately: it rolls the status back and surfaces the error.
*)
< true* . "APP_PARTIAL_SUBMISSION" .
  (not "SAVE_SUBMISSION !CRS_0 !ASN_0 !PLACEHOLDER")* .
  "SUBMISSION_STATUS !ASN_0 !SUBMITTED_FG" > true
